            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "+1, and +1 to include U+FF07.\n\nThere are several other characters listed with U+0027 APOSTROPHE in http://www.unicode.org/charts/PDF/U0000.pdf that could be interpreted visually as an English apostrophe, e.g. U+02BC MODIFIER LETTER APOSTROPHE, but it would be unusual for people to use those characters as apostrophes in English text, so I think it would be fine to exclude them.  (By contrast, the Unicode standard says that U+2019 is the *preferred* apostrophe form.)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2012-02-02T20:47:49.492+0000",
          "updated": "2012-02-02T20:47:49.492+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12540991/comment/13199217",
          "id": "13199217",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Thats my thoughts exactly Steven.\n\nI think by default we should go with U+0027 and U+2019 (and as i mentioned, either FF07 or not, its less important). \n\nAs far as other look-alikes, sure it could happen, BUT the user could just place ASCIIFoldingFilter before\nEnglishPossessiveFilter if they want that more brutal behavior... thats a more lossy normalization that I \ndon't think we should do by default...",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2012-02-02T21:01:55.140+0000",
          "updated": "2012-02-02T21:01:55.140+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12540991/comment/13199262",
          "id": "13199262",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dcroley",
            "name": "dcroley",
            "key": "dcroley",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
